 "what_this_is": "Two safeguards measured against live Amazon Bedrock: the deployed guardrail, called through apply_guardrail on the INPUT direction, and the turn reader, called through the same structured path a family message takes. The lines are in tests/distress_corpus.py and the run is scripts/run_distress_probe.py, at three samples a line. The reader arm is reported for both models the structured role can carry: the default in config/models.py and the one deploy/agentcore/runtime.yaml binds. The before rows are the same script's reader arm against the branch point, where distress was not a value the schema allowed. The first_reading rows are the first version of the distress wording, on the default model, and are kept because they are the reason the wording changed.",
 "what_this_is_not": "Not a safety rate and not a clinical instrument. Eighteen authored lines at three samples, in one language, on one day, is a probe of whether a written sentence reaches an adult at all -- not a measure of how often a real child's words would. No child wrote any of these lines, no clinician labelled them, and the corpus was written by the same person who wrote the prompt it tests. It says nothing about the sentences nobody thought to write down.",
